The bug was caused by a logic error in the permission check for device access in the cgroup setup, where the condition incorrectly allowed write permissions only when the `readonly` flag was true, leading to failures in starting any domain.



Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:

    if (!src->path || !virStorageSourceIsLocalStorage(src)) {
        VIR_DEBUG("Not updating cgroups for disk path '%s', type: %s",
                  NULLSTR(src->path), virStorageTypeToString(src->type));
        return 0;
    }

    if (!src->readonly && !forceReadonly)
